libnet: no <values.h> on android

net_util_md.c reaches for the legacy SysV header <values.h>, which bionic does
not ship:

  net_util_md.c:39:10: fatal error: 'values.h' file not found

MAXINT is the only thing it takes from there, and the file already has a
fallback for it -- the _ALLBSD_SOURCE branch defines MAXINT from INT_MAX.
Give android the same treatment in its own branch rather than folding it into
the BSD one, which also pulls <sys/param.h> and <sys/sysctl.h>; sysctl is not
something to lean on in a current NDK.

diff --git a/jdk/src/solaris/native/java/net/net_util_md.c b/jdk/src/solaris/native/java/net/net_util_md.c
index bd0bd8c..d849c67 100644
--- a/jdk/src/solaris/native/java/net/net_util_md.c
+++ b/jdk/src/solaris/native/java/net/net_util_md.c
@@ -35,7 +35,13 @@
 #include <dlfcn.h>
 #include <sys/time.h>
 
-#ifndef _ALLBSD_SOURCE
+#if defined(__ANDROID__)
+/* bionic has no <values.h>; MAXINT is all this file wants from it. */
+#include <limits.h>
+#ifndef MAXINT
+#define MAXINT INT_MAX
+#endif
+#elif !defined(_ALLBSD_SOURCE)
 #include <values.h>
 #else
 #include <limits.h>
